===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|hangen}}, {{m|enm|hongen}}, from a fusion of {{inh|en|ang|hōn||to hang, be hanging|pos=intransitive verb}} and {{m|ang|hangian|t=to hang, cause to hang|pos=transitive verb}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*hą̄han}} and {{m|gmw-pro|*hangēn}}; also probably influenced by {{cog|non|hengja|t=to suspend}} and {{m|non|hanga|t=to be suspended}}; all from {{der|en|gem-pro|*hanhaną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*hangāną}} (compare {{cog|nl|hangen}}, {{cog|nds|hangen}} and {{m|nds|hängen}}, {{cog|de|hängen}}, {{cog|nb|henge}}, {{cog|nn|henga}}), from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ḱenk-||to waver, be in suspense}} (compare {{cog|got|𐌷𐌰𐌷𐌰𐌽|tr=hāhan}}, {{cog|hit|𒂵𒀀𒀭𒂵|ts=kānk-|t=to hang}}, {{cog|sa|शङ्कते||is in doubt, hesitates|tr=śáṅkate}}, {{cog|la|cūnctārī||to delay}}).

