# {{lb|en|intransitive|figuratively}} To [[remain]] persistently in one's thoughts.
#* {{RQ:Wells Time Machine|X||Exploring, I found another short gallery running transversely to the first. This appeared to be devoted to minerals, and the sight of a block of sulphur set my mind running on gunpowder. But I could find no saltpeter; indeed no nitrates of any kind. Doubtless they had deliquesced ages ago. Yet the sulphur '''hung''' in my mind and set up a train of thinking.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To prevent from reaching a decision, especially by refusing to join in a verdict that must be unanimous.
#: {{ux|en|One obstinate juror can '''hang''' a jury.}}
